        </div>
        <div class="meal-card">
          <div class="meal-header"><div class="meal-time">3–4pm</div><div class="meal-name">🥛 Afternoon Shake</div><div class="meal-macros"><span class="macro-pill mp-cal">~120 cal</span><span class="macro-pill mp-p">25g protein</span></div></div>
          <div class="meal-body">
            <div class="food-row"><div><div class="food-name">Whey — Water Only</div><div class="food-note">Keep it lean today. No banana alongside.</div></div><div class="food-portion">1 scoop</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="meal-card">
          <div class="meal-header"><div class="meal-time">6:30pm</div><div class="meal-name">🍽️ Dinner — Protein + Veg Only</div><div class="meal-macros"><span class="macro-pill mp-cal">~420 cal</span><span class="macro-pill mp-p">50g protein</span></div></div>
          <div class="meal-body">
            <div class="food-row"><div><div class="food-name">Lean Protein (Chicken, Turkey, or White Fish preferred)</div><div class="food-note">Leaner cuts today — lower fat than beef or salmon on a rest day</div></div><div class="food-portion">2 palms</div></div>
            <div class="food-row"><div><div class="food-name">Vegetables — Fill the Plate</div><div class="food-note">Unlimited. This replaces the volume you're losing by skipping starch.</div></div><div class="food-portion">Unlimited</div></div>
            <div class="food-row"><div><div class="food-name">NO Starch Tonight</div><div class="food-note">No rice, no potato, no bread. You didn't earn the glycogen refill today.</div></div><div class="food-portion">Skip it</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="meal-card">
          <div class="meal-header"><div class="meal-time">9pm</div><div class="meal-name">🍨 Dessert — Greek Yogurt</div><div class="meal-macros"><span class="macro-pill mp-cal">~110 cal</span><span class="macro-pill mp-p">20g protein</span></div></div>
          <div class="meal-body">
            <div class="food-row"><div><div class="food-name">0% Plain Greek Yogurt</div><div class="food-note">More important on rest days — overnight protein synthesis continues even without training. This feeds it. Berries or cinnamon to taste.</div></div><div class="food-portion">¾ cup</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- DINNERS -->
    <div class="submodule" id="sub-dinners">
      <div class="note-box green"><strong>Same structure every dinner:</strong> 2 palm-sized portions of protein + unlimited veg + 1 fist of starch on training days only. Partner cooking? Show them this page.</div>
      <div class="slabel green" style="margin-top:0">Lean — Use Most Often</div>
      <div class="dinner-grid">
        <div class="dinner-card"><div class="dinner-protein">🍗 Chicken Breast</div><div class="dinner-detail">Grill, bake, or pan-sear. Season freely — salt, garlic, paprika, cumin. No cream sauces.</div><div class="dinner-macros"><span class="dp dp-cal">~280 cal</span><span class="dp dp-p">53g protein</span></div></div>
        <div class="dinner-card"><div class="dinner-protein">🦃 Ground Turkey (93%)</div><div class="dinner-detail">Taco bowls (no tortilla), stir fry, or simple skillet with peppers and onions.</div><div class="dinner-macros"><span class="dp dp-cal">~260 cal</span><span class="dp dp-p">47g protein</span></div></div>
        <div class="dinner-card"><div class="dinner-protein">🐟 White Fish</div><div class="dinner-detail">Tilapia, cod, halibut. Bake or pan-fry. Lemon, salt, herbs. Fast to cook, very lean.</div><div class="dinner-macros"><span class="dp dp-cal">~200 cal</span><span class="dp dp-p">42g protein</span></div></div>
        <div class="dinner-card"><div class="dinner-protein">🥩 Pork Tenderloin</div><div class="dinner-detail">Leanest cut of pork. Marinate and roast. Rivals chicken breast in protein per calorie.</div><div class="dinner-macros"><span class="dp dp-cal">~250 cal</span><span class="dp dp-p">46g protein</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="slabel orange">Moderate — 2–3x Per Week</div>
      <div class="dinner-grid">
        <div class="dinner-card"><div class="dinner-protein">🍣 Salmon</div><div class="dinner-detail">Higher fat but omega-3s reduce inflammation from training. Worth the extra calories 2–3x/week. 6oz fillet.</div><div class="dinner-macros"><span class="dp dp-cal">~370 cal</span><span class="dp dp-p">40g protein</span></div></div>
        <div class="dinner-card"><div class="dinner-protein">🥩 Lean Ground Beef (93%)</div><div class="dinner-detail">Taco bowl, stir fry, or burger patty (no bun). More satiating than turkey — good for high hunger days.</div><div class="dinner-macros"><span class="dp dp-cal">~320 cal</span><span class="dp dp-p">42g protein</span></div></div>
        <div class="dinner-card"><div class="dinner-protein">🥩 Steak — Sirloin or Flank</div><div class="dinner-detail">Sirloin or flank only, skip ribeye during the cut. 6oz max. Best post-workout or weekends.</div><div class="dinner-macros"><span class="dp dp-cal">~340 cal</span><span class="dp dp-p">44g protein</span></div></div>
        <div class="dinner-card"><div class="dinner-protein">🍗 Chicken Thighs (Skin Off)</div><div class="dinner-detail">More flavor than breast, slightly higher fat. Skin off keeps it reasonable. Great when someone else is cooking.</div><div class="dinner-macros"><span class="dp dp-cal">~300 cal</span><span class="dp dp-p">38g protein</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="slabel green">Unlimited Veg — Fill the Plate</div>
      <div class="note-box green" style="margin-bottom:0">Broccoli · Asparagus · Green Beans · Zucchini · Spinach · Bell Peppers · Cauliflower · Brussels Sprouts · Cucumber · Tomatoes · Mushrooms<br><br><strong>Cook with olive oil or butter — 1 thumb max. Season aggressively. Bland food kills compliance.</strong></div>
    </div>

    <!-- RULES -->
    <div class="submodule" id="sub-rules">
      <div class="slabel green" style="margin-top:0">Hand Portion Guide — Your Calorie Counter</div>
      <div class="portion-grid">
        <div class="portion-card"><div class="portion-emoji">✊</div><div class="portion-name">Protein</div><div class="portion-desc">2 palm-sized portions per meal. Thickness counts, not just area.</div><div class="portion-example">~6oz chicken, 2 eggs, 1 can sardines</div></div>
        <div class="portion-card"><div class="portion-emoji">🤜</div><div class="portion-name">Starch</div><div class="portion-desc">1 fist per meal. Training days only at dinner. Always at breakfast.</div><div class="portion-example">½ cup rice, 1 potato, ½ cup oats</div></div>
        <div class="portion-card"><div class="portion-emoji">👍</div><div class="portion-name">Fat</div><div class="portion-desc">1 thumb per meal max. Oils, butter, dressings, avocado.</div><div class="portion-example">1 tsp olive oil, small pat butter</div></div>
        <div class="portion-card"><div class="portion-emoji">🖐️</div><div class="portion-name">Vegetables</div><div class="portion-desc">2+ fistfuls every meal. Unlimited. Non-starchy only.</div><div class="portion-example">Broccoli, spinach, zucchini, peppers</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="slabel green">Non-Negotiable Rules</div>
      <div class="rule-grid">
        <div class="rule-card rule-green"><strong>Protein Every Single Meal</strong><p>Never eat without a protein source. This one habit gets you to 200g/day automatically — no app required.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card rule-orange"><strong>Carbs Around Training Only</strong><p>Banana pre-gym, fruit post-gym, starch at dinner on training days. Rest days — oats at breakfast only. Carbs are fuel, not a right.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card rule-blue"><strong>2 Whey Scoops Daily</strong><p>One pre-gym, one mid-afternoon. 50g protein added to your day with zero cooking. Both training and rest days.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card rule-green"><strong>2 Sardine Cans at Lunch</strong><p>Every workday without exception. Already at the office. 46g protein, omega-3s, zero carbs. The cornerstone of your work nutrition.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card rule-red"><strong>No Liquid Calories</strong><p>No juice, soda, specialty coffee, sports drinks. Black coffee, water, sparkling water, and whey only. Liquid calories are invisible and will silently destroy this cut.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card rule-yellow"><strong>Hunger = More Protein First</strong><p>If genuinely hungry between meals, reach for protein — another shake, Greek yogurt, cottage cheese. Never a carb-only snack. Hunger usually means the last meal was low on protein.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="slabel red">Silent Cut Killers</div>
      <div class="rule-grid">
        <div class="rule-card rule-red"><strong>Flavored Oats / Instant Packets</strong><p>20–25g added sugar per packet. Plain rolled oats only.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card rule-red"><strong>Flavored Yogurt</strong><p>Regular yogurt is 20–30g sugar. 0% plain Greek only. Add berries for flavor.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card rule-red"><strong>Sauces and Dressings</strong><p>BBQ, ranch, teriyaki = 100–200 invisible cal per serving. Use hot sauce, mustard, salsa, lemon.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card rule-red"><strong>Cooking Oil Overuse</strong><p>A "drizzle" can be 200+ cal. Use a measured teaspoon or cooking spray every time.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- WEEKEND -->
    <div class="submodule" id="sub-weekend">
      <div class="note-box"><strong>A few drinks Saturday won't ruin this cut.</strong> Unmanaged drinking will. The strategy is earning the drinks by being leaner on Saturday's food — not white-knuckling abstinence.</div>
      <div class="slabel yellow">Drink Calorie Reference</div>
      <div class="alcohol-card">
        <div class="alcohol-hdr">📊 Know What You're Drinking</div>
        <div class="drink-row"><span>Light Beer (12oz)</span><span class="drink-cal">~100 cal</span></div>
        <div class="drink-row"><span>Regular Beer (12oz)</span><span class="drink-cal">~150 cal</span></div>
        <div class="drink-row"><span>Spirits — Whiskey, Vodka, Tequila (1.5oz)</span><span class="drink-cal">~100 cal</span></div>
        <div class="drink-row"><span>Spirits + Soda Water (best choice)</span><span class="drink-cal">~100 cal total</span></div>
        <div class="drink-row"><span>Dry Red or White Wine (5oz)</span><span class="drink-cal">~120 cal</span></div>
        <div class="drink-row"><span>Craft IPA (12oz)</span><span class="drink-cal">~200–250 cal</span></div>
        <div class="drink-row"><span>Mixed cocktails (margarita, rum & coke)</span><span class="drink-cal">~200–400 cal — avoid</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="slabel yellow">Saturday Protocol</div>
      <div class="rule-grid">
        <div class="rule-card rule-yellow"><strong>Budget 3 Drinks Max</strong><p>3 light beers or spirits = ~300–350 cal. Manageable. 6+ drinks = 600–900 cal on top of food = cut paused for the week.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card rule-yellow"><strong>Eat Before You Drink</strong><p>High protein dinner before going out. Full stomach slows absorption, reduces overconsumption, and prevents 2am food decisions.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card rule-orange"><strong>Skip Dinner Starch That Day</strong><p>Frees up ~100 cal to put toward drinks. Small trade-off, big compliance win for the evening.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card rule-orange"><strong>Avoid the Drunk Food Trap</strong><p>This is where cuts die — not the drinks, but the 2am pizza. Decide before you leave the house: no late-night food. That one decision saves 1,000+ calories.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card rule-blue"><strong>Best Drink Choices</strong><p>Vodka / tequila / whiskey + soda water + lime. Dry red wine. Light beer. Lowest calorie, lowest sugar. Avoid IPAs, cocktails, and anything with juice or syrup.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-card rule-green"><strong>Sunday is a Reset, Not a Punishment</strong><p>Back on the rest day protocol immediately. One evening of drinks + a clean Sunday does almost zero measurable damage to 6 weeks of results.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════════════ PHASES ═══════════════ -->
  <div class="module" id="module-phases">
    <div class="slabel" style="margin-top:0">6-Week Progression Map</div>
    <div class="phase-strip">
      <div class="phase-card ph-1"><div class="phase-name">Foundation</div><div class="phase-wks">Weeks 1–2</div></div>
      <div class="phase-card ph-2"><div class="phase-name">Accelerate</div><div class="phase-wks">Weeks 3–4</div></div>
      <div class="phase-card ph-3"><div class="phase-name">Peak</div><div class="phase-wks">Weeks 5–6</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="slabel">Weeks 1–2 · Foundation</div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Calories</div><div class="ex-note">2,300/day — let the body adapt before tightening the deficit</div></div><div class="ex-sets">~500 deficit</div></div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Cardio</div><div class="ex-note">Dog walks AM + PM · Gym finishers every session · ~60–70 active min/day total</div></div><div class="ex-sets">Base volume</div></div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Lifting</div><div class="ex-note">Establish working weights across all 6 sessions. Form, feel, and rhythm of the rolling cycle.</div></div><div class="ex-sets">Learn the cycle</div></div>
    <div class="slabel">Weeks 3–4 · Acceleration</div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Calories</div><div class="ex-note">2,150/day — tighten now that adaptation is complete</div></div><div class="ex-sets">~650 deficit</div></div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Cardio Add-On</div><div class="ex-note">1 lunch jog per cycle (20–25 min from home). Dog walks extend to 30 min each.</div></div><div class="ex-sets">+1 jog/cycle</div></div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Lifting Density</div><div class="ex-note">Rest periods drop to 60–90s. Add one drop set per session on the primary compound.</div></div><div class="ex-sets">Higher density</div></div>
    <div class="slabel">Weeks 5–6 · Peak</div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Calories</div><div class="ex-note">2,050/day — deeper but NEVER sacrifice protein. Cut carbs, protect protein.</div></div><div class="ex-sets">~750 deficit</div></div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Cardio Add-On</div><div class="ex-note">2 lunch jogs per cycle. Dog walks 30+ min. Maximum daily steps.</div></div><div class="ex-sets">+2 jogs/cycle</div></div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Lifting</div><div class="ex-note">HOLD working weights. Never reduce load — the muscle needs progressive stimulus to stay.</div></div><div class="ex-sets">Hold the load</div></div>
    <div class="slabel red">April 25–May 1 · Peak Week</div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Mon–Thu — Water Load + Low Sodium</div><div class="ex-note">1.5 gallons water/day · Cut added sodium · Flush subcutaneous water retention</div></div><div class="ex-sets">Days 1–4</div></div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Friday — Carb Refeed</div><div class="ex-note">Add 100g clean carbs (rice, oats) on top of normal intake. Refills glycogen — muscles look full not flat.</div></div><div class="ex-sets">Day 5</div></div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Sat/Sun — The Payoff</div><div class="ex-note">Maintenance calories. Less water, full muscles. This is when you look your absolute best.</div></div><div class="ex-sets">Game day 🔥</div></div>
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════════════ CARDIO ═══════════════ -->
  <div class="module" id="module-cardio">
    <div class="slabel" style="margin-top:0">Daily Cardio Stack</div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">🌅 Morning Dog Walk — Fasted</div><div class="ex-note">Before breakfast. Fasted LISS oxidizes ~20% more fat as fuel (Howarth et al.). 20–30 min brisk. Zero extra time cost.</div></div><div class="ex-sets">~150 cal</div></div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">💪 Gym HIIT Finisher — Post Lift</div><div class="ex-note">15 min at end of every session. Rower, bike, or treadmill. Creates EPOC — metabolism elevated 12–24 hrs after.</div></div><div class="ex-sets">~150 cal</div></div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">🌆 Evening Dog Walk — Post Dinner</div><div class="ex-note">Post-meal walking significantly blunts glucose spikes and improves insulin sensitivity. 20–30 min. One of the most research-backed fat loss habits you can build.</div></div><div class="ex-sets">~120 cal</div></div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">🏃 Lunch Jog — From Home</div><div class="ex-note">Wks 3–4: 1x per cycle. Wks 5–6: 2x per cycle. 20–25 min moderate pace. Replaces gym finisher those days.</div></div><div class="ex-sets">~250 cal</div></div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">👟 Daily Step Goal</div><div class="ex-note">10,000–12,000 steps. NEAT is massively underestimated. Dog walks alone get you most of the way there every single day.</div></div><div class="ex-sets">10–12k steps</div></div>
    <div class="slabel">Weekly Calorie Burn From Cardio Alone</div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Dog Walks</div><div class="ex-note">~270 cal/day × 7 days</div></div><div class="ex-sets">~1,900/wk</div></div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Gym HIIT Finishers × 6 sessions</div><div class="ex-note">~150 cal each</div></div><div class="ex-sets">~900/wk</div></div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Lunch Jogs (Wks 5–6)</div><div class="ex-note">2 per cycle × ~250 cal</div></div><div class="ex-sets">~500/wk</div></div>
    <div class="ex-row"><div><div class="ex-name">Total Weekly Cardio Burn (Peak)</div><div class="ex-note">On top of your caloric deficit — this is the accelerant</div></div><div class="ex-sets">~3,300 cal</div></div>
    <div class="slabel">HIIT vs LISS — Why Both</div>
    <div class="principle-grid">
      <div class="principle"><strong>Why HIIT Finishers</strong>EPOC keeps metabolism elevated 12–24 hrs post session. Tremblay et al.: HIIT produces significantly greater fat loss than equivalent steady state — in less time.</div>
      <div class="principle"><strong>Why Fasted Morning Walks</strong>At low intensity in a fasted state, the body preferentially burns fat. Your dog makes this automatic every morning — zero willpower required.</div>
      <div class="principle"><strong>Why NOT Just Run Every Day</strong>High volume running + large deficit + heavy lifting = cortisol spike = muscle breakdown. Walks + HIIT finishers burn serious calories without wrecking recovery.</div>
      <div class="principle"><strong>Post-Dinner Walk Science</strong>Colberg et al.: Even a 15-minute post-meal walk significantly reduces blood glucose response. Lower glucose = lower insulin = more fat oxidation overnight.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<script>
function showModule(name, btn) {
  document.querySelectorAll('.module').forEach(m => m.classList.remove('active'));
  document.querySelectorAll('.top-nav-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));
  document.getElementById('module-' + name).classList.add('active');
  btn.classList.add('active');
}
function showSub(name, btn) {
  document.querySelectorAll('.submodule').forEach(s => s.classList.remove('active'));
  document.querySelectorAll('.sub-nav-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));
  document.getElementById('sub-' + name).classList.add('active');
  btn.classList.add('active');
}
function showDay(day, btn) {
  // find parent module/submodule and only deactivate panels within it
  const panels = btn.closest('.day-tabs').nextElementSibling ? btn.closest('.module, .submodule') : document;
  const container = btn.closest('.module') || btn.closest('.submodule') || document;
  container.querySelectorAll('.day-panel').forEach(p => p.classList.remove('active'));
  container.querySelectorAll('.day-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));
  document.getElementById('day-' + day).classList.add('active');
  btn.classList.add('active');
}
function jumpToDay(day, cycleIdx) {
  // activate training module
  document.querySelectorAll('.module').forEach(m => m.classList.remove('active'));
  document.querySelectorAll('.top-nav-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));
  document.getElementById('module-training').classList.add('active');
  document.querySelectorAll('.top-nav-btn')[0].classList.add('active');
  // activate day
  document.querySelectorAll('.day-panel').forEach(p => p.classList.remove('active'));
  document.querySelectorAll('#module-training .day-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));
  document.getElementById('day-' + day).classList.add('active');
  document.getElementById('tab-' + day).classList.add('active');
  // update cycle highlight
  document.querySelectorAll('.cycle-day').forEach((d, i) => d.classList.toggle('active-cyc', i === cycleIdx));
  window.scrollTo({top: 0, behavior: 'smooth'});
}
</script>
